---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Crumbs from "../components/Crumbs.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE.url + "/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Services", item: SITE.url + "/services" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Data & Analytics project management", item: SITE.url + "/data-project-management-change-leadership" },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Analytics project management | Alluvium"
  description="The work stalls when nobody owns the decisions. We run the dashboard project to a finish the business will actually use."
  canonicalPath="/data-project-management-change-leadership"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <Crumbs crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { href: "/services", label: "Services" }, { label: "Data & Analytics project management" }]} />
        <p class="kicker">Project leadership</p>
        <h1>Someone has to own the dashboard project</h1>
        <p class="lede">The work stalls when nobody owns the decisions. We run it to a finish the business will actually use.</p>
        <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>The build can look done and still sit unused</h2>
        <p>Scope keeps moving. Nobody owns the refresh. Nobody owns who can see which rows. The training is a slide, and it happens after the meeting that needed the report.</p>
        <p>Finance still opens the old file. The model was not the failure. The failure is that no one owned the decisions that get the report used.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>They work in the report, not on a slide</h2>
        <p>The slide sits behind the page. The people who have to use the number are in the report.</p>
        <figure>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 680 320" role="img" aria-label="A slide of text sits behind a large report. Two pointers rest on the report.">
        <rect x="28" y="58" width="220" height="236" rx="4" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="92" x2="156" y2="92" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="116" x2="150" y2="116" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="134" x2="142" y2="134" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="152" x2="154" y2="152" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="170" x2="128" y2="170" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>

        <rect x="176" y="24" width="472" height="276" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2.5"/>
        <line x1="196" y1="72" x2="628" y2="72" stroke="#e7f1f8" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <rect x="200" y="88" width="56" height="16" rx="8" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="266" y="88" width="56" height="16" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="332" y="88" width="56" height="16" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="200" y1="256" x2="620" y2="256" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="214" y="196" width="32" height="60" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="270" y="156" width="32" height="100" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="326" y="176" width="32" height="80" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.72"/>
        <rect x="382" y="116" width="32" height="140" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
        <rect x="438" y="166" width="32" height="90" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="494" y="206" width="32" height="50" fill="#e7f1f8" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="550" y="186" width="32" height="70" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <path d="M306 132 l0 20 5 0 4 9 4-2-4-9 6 0 z" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <path d="M418 112 l0 24 6 0 5 11 5-2.5-5-11 7 0 z" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
      </svg>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What we hold until people use it</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card"><h3>Scope</h3><p>Tied to the decision the report has to support. A new request does not join the work by default.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Owners</h3><p>A name for the team, a name for keeping the report current, and a name for who can see which rows.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>The calendar</h3><p>A timeline the business can see, including when people are told what changed.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Training</h3><p>On the report, before the meeting that needs it, and checked after. Not assumed.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p>You get a Power BI project people use. Not a file that was only handed over.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <RelatedLinks
      services={[
        { href: "/power-bi-training", label: "Power BI training" },
        { href: "/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap", label: "Analytics strategy roadmap" },
        { href: "/managed-advisory-retainer", label: "Managed advisory retainer" },
      ]}
      posts={[
        { href: "/blog/analytics-programs-fail-in-delivery", label: "Analytics programs fail in delivery" },
        { href: "/blog/pmo-should-own-the-analytics-backlog", label: "PMO should own the analytics backlog" },
        { href: "/blog/the-meeting-after-go-live", label: "The meeting after go-live" },
      ]}
    />
    <CtaBand heading="Name the decision nobody owns." text="Book a session. We will see whether the gap is the plan, the owners, or the fact that nobody opens the report." />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
